Subject: [PATCH] Scope original-prompt recovery to fixed input requests

Base: candidate-38 private decoder recovery. Actual streaming-input sessions can change CED floors and per-request settings across phases. A single original or current prompt boundary does not reproduce that history, so retain their existing recovery policy. Ordinary stateless chat turns and output-only streaming retain the fix.

Carry the durable streaming-queue identity to the worker even after the final input sentinel clears resumable. Add cache admission and worker-policy tests for active and ended input streams. Numerical phase tests cover append lengths 1/2/127/128/129/256. Native and full-model qualification remain pending; this does not claim streaming-input recovery correctness. Upstream status: draft fork PR6.
